From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cloud Browser WebRTC Authors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0001/0001] cloud-browser: expose embedder hook for WebRTC
 video encoder factory

Adds a virtual on content::ContentBrowserClient that lets an embedder
return a webrtc::VideoEncoderFactory; content::PeerConnectionDependency
Factory consults it before falling back to its built-in factory.

Why this patch exists:
- Our cloud-browser worker (//cloud-browser/capture/build-integration/
  BUILD.gn) needs to plug CloudBrowserVideoEncoderFactory (T19 / T35 /
  T36) into the libwebrtc PeerConnectionFactory used inside Chromium.
- Chromium does not currently surface the
  PeerConnectionFactoryDependencies::video_encoder_factory slot to
  embedders; CreatePeerConnectionFactory_w() owns the assignment
  internally.
- The least-invasive alternative — patching the assignment site to
  read a global — would force every embedder to share a factory.
  A virtual on ContentBrowserClient is the standard Chromium shape
  for "let embedders override this single decision."

Why not avoid the patch:
- Investigated using BLINK_VIDEO_ENCODER_FACTORY_FOR_TESTING /
  similar test-only seams: those are gated on test-only build flags
  and not load-bearing for production.
- A separate process running libwebrtc directly (no Chromium) was
  ruled out by the Phase 2 capture design (see
  docs/capture/framesink-design.md §2 — the embedder approach beats
  the patch-on-top approach on latency and maintainability).

Upstream considerations:
- This is the kind of seam Chromium has historically been willing to
  accept upstream when there is a non-test embedder asking for it.
  Track an upstream bug as a follow-up; until that lands the patch
  rebases each release branch (low touch — the diff is tiny and the
  files churn slowly).

Touched files:
- content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h
- content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc
- third_party/blink/renderer/modules/peerconnection/
    peer_connection_dependency_factory.cc

Reference paths against pinned branch refs/branch-heads/<NNNN>; the
context lines are illustrative — re-resolve on each roll. The shape
of the diff (one virtual, one consultation site) does not change.

TODO(T17-build-env): apply against the pinned tree and confirm the
